{% comment %}
  Collection hero (Figma: V2 Birthday Treats Occasion collection page → Hero,
  491:19940, with the trail above it at 491:19971).

  A rounded banner inset by the page gutter: the collection's photograph behind, a
  star, the collection's name in two tones and the sentence under it. The card sits
  inside the page column rather than running to the window edge, which is what the
  20px radius is for.

  The words are the template's, not the collection's. The heading and the copy are
  ordinary [_ui-heading] and [_ui-text] blocks a merchant types into — this is a
  banner laid out per template, the way any other section is.

  The picture is the collection's, but through a metafield of its own and not through
  `collection.image`. That field is spoken for in production, and a banner and a
  thumbnail are not the same picture anyway: one is 3.37:1 with room in the middle for
  a heading, the other is whatever the catalogue needs.

  So `custom.hero_image` on the collection, with the section's picker behind it — the
  metafield is the per-collection answer and the picker is the floor for a template
  eight collections share. That is the bargain `docs/section-settings.md` describes for
  the product page, and a blank metafield leaves the section's own picture standing.
  The key is a setting rather than a constant, so the name is the merchant's and this
  file is not the only place it is written down.

  Both blocks can read the collection instead: their `source` setting offers
  `collection_title` and `collection_description`, and on that path the two-tone accent
  comes from the collection's `custom.title_accent` metafield. That is what one shared
  `templates/collection.json` would want if the shop ever fills those fields in. It is
  a switch, not the default, because a banner is editorial: the words that sell a
  Birthday page are rarely the words in its collection description, and the picture
  filed against a collection is a product shot rather than a banner.

  A phone gets its own picker, as `docs/section-settings.md` asks for every image.
  The banner is drawn 3.37:1 and a phone's card is nearer 1.3:1, so `cover` throws
  away about three fifths of the width — on this one that is the box of treats at one
  end and the cake at the other, leaving the pale middle the words sit on. Legible,
  and empty. A crop cut for the shape belongs in the second picker rather than in a
  rule that squeezes the first.

  The two are one `<picture>` and not two `<img>`s behind a media query: a browser
  picks one source and downloads one file, where the display-toggle version fetches
  both and shows one.

  The file draws no scrim, and the default is no scrim — the banner it draws is a pale
  purpose-made photograph the black heading sits on happily. The switch is there for a
  shop that hangs a busier picture behind the same words.

  The trail's middle step is written out rather than taken from a resource. A
  collection's parent here is a nav item — "Shop Treats" — which is not a thing with
  a `.title` and a `.url` that Liquid will hand over, so [ui-breadcrumb] takes the
  two strings instead.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign hero_collection = collection
  if request.visual_preview_mode and hero_collection == blank
    assign hero_collection = collections.all
  endif

  assign hero_image = section.settings.image
  assign hero_image_mobile = section.settings.image_mobile

  # The collection's own banner wins over the template's. `.value` is what a
  # file_reference hands back — the metafield object itself is not an image, and
  # asking it for a URL renders nothing rather than failing loudly.
  assign image_key = section.settings.image_metafield
  if image_key != blank
    assign from_collection = hero_collection.metafields.custom[image_key].value
    if from_collection != blank
      assign hero_image = from_collection
    endif
  endif

  assign image_key_mobile = section.settings.image_mobile_metafield
  if image_key_mobile != blank
    assign from_collection_mobile = hero_collection.metafields.custom[image_key_mobile].value
    if from_collection_mobile != blank
      assign hero_image_mobile = from_collection_mobile
    endif
  endif

  # Either picker on its own is a whole banner. Only both empty holds the frame.
  if hero_image == blank
    assign hero_image = hero_image_mobile
  endif
-%}

<div
  class="section section--{{ section.settings.section_width }} spacing-style color-{{ section.settings.color_scheme }}"
  style="{% render 'spacing-style', settings: section.settings %}"
  data-testid="collection-hero-{{ section.id }}"
  {{ section.shopify_attributes }}
>
  <div
    class="collection-hero"
    style="
      --collection-hero-height: {{ section.settings.height_mobile }}px;
      --collection-hero-height-desktop: {{ section.settings.height }}px;
    "
  >
    {%- if section.settings.show_breadcrumb -%}
      {% render 'ui-breadcrumb',
        parent_title: section.settings.parent_title,
        parent_url: section.settings.parent_link,
        current: hero_collection.title,
        class: 'collection-hero__breadcrumb'
      %}
    {%- endif -%}

    <div class="collection-hero__card">
      <div class="collection-hero__media" aria-hidden="true">
        {%- if hero_image != blank -%}
          <picture>
            {%- if hero_image_mobile != blank -%}
              <source
                media="(max-width: 749px)"
                srcset="
                  {{ hero_image_mobile | image_url: width: 750 }} 1x,
                  {{ hero_image_mobile | image_url: width: 1500 }} 2x
                "
              >
            {%- endif -%}
            {% render 'image', image: hero_image, height: 760, class: 'collection-hero__image' %}
          </picture>
        {%- else -%}
          {%- comment -%} Photography is not in yet; hold the frame so the band reads true. {%- endcomment -%}
          <span class="collection-hero__image collection-hero__image--placeholder"></span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- if section.settings.show_scrim -%}
        <span
          class="collection-hero__scrim"
          style="--collection-hero-scrim: {{ section.settings.scrim_opacity | divided_by: 100.0 }};"
          aria-hidden="true"
        ></span>
      {%- endif -%}

      <div class="collection-hero__content">
        {%- if section.settings.show_star -%}
          <span class="collection-hero__star" aria-hidden="true">
            {{- 'icon-ui-sparkle.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
          </span>
        {%- endif -%}

        <div class="collection-hero__text">
          {% content_for 'blocks' %}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
  /* Collection hero. Mobile first; the drawn height arrives at 750px. */
  .collection-hero {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
  }

  .collection-hero__card {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    overflow: hidden;

    /*
     * A floor, not a height. The file draws 380 with two short lines in it; a
     * collection whose sentence runs longer grows the card rather than spilling
     * out of it.
     */
    min-block-size: var(--collection-hero-height, 260px);
    padding-block: 24px 32px;
    padding-inline: var(--ui-page-margin);
    border-radius: var(--collection-hero-radius, 20px);
  }

  /*
   * The photograph is a layer under the words rather than a `background-image`, so
   * it can be a responsive `<img>` with a srcset the browser picks from. Taken out
   * of the accessibility tree with the wrapper's `aria-hidden`: it is scenery, and
   * the heading beside it already says what the page is.
   */
  .collection-hero__media {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 0;
  }

  .collection-hero__media picture {
    display: block;
    inline-size: 100%;
    block-size: 100%;
  }

  .collection-hero__image {
    display: block;
    inline-size: 100%;
    block-size: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .collection-hero__image--placeholder {
    background-color: var(--ui-color-light-blue);
  }

  /*
   * White rather than black: the heading over it is drawn black and purple, so what
   * the photograph has to be pushed towards is paper, not night.
   */
  .collection-hero__scrim {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 0;
    background-color: rgb(255 255 255 / var(--collection-hero-scrim, 0.6));
  }

  .collection-hero__content {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--collection-hero-gap, 24px);
    inline-size: 100%;
  }

  .collection-hero__star {
    display: block;
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    inline-size: var(--collection-hero-star, 32px);
    block-size: var(--collection-hero-star, 32px);
    color: var(--ui-color-primary);
  }

  .collection-hero__star > svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
  }

  .collection-hero__text {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 16px;
    inline-size: 100%;

    /*
     * The two pieces of copy are drawn 410 and 416 wide inside a 1280 card, which
     * is a measure rather than a preference — a headline set across the whole card
     * is a line nobody finishes. Handed down, so a block that sets its own wins.
     */
    --ui-heading-max-width: 440px;
    --ui-text-max-width: 440px;

    text-align: center;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .collection-hero {
      gap: 24px;
    }

    .collection-hero__card {
      --collection-hero-gap: 48px;

      min-block-size: var(--collection-hero-height-desktop, 380px);
      padding-block: 24px 64px;
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Collection hero",
  "tag": "section",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "_ui-heading"
    },
    {
      "type": "_ui-text"
    }
  ],
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:content.media"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "image",
      "label": "Banner, every collection",
      "info": "The floor for a template every collection shares. A collection that fills in its own metafield below wins over this. With neither, the frame is held with a placeholder."
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "image_mobile",
      "label": "Banner on mobile, every collection",
      "info": "A crop cut for the taller shape a phone gives the banner. Left empty, the desktop picture is centre-cropped and loses about three fifths of its width."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Per collection"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Add these under Settings → Custom data → Collections as File metafields that accept images, then fill them in per collection. A collection that leaves one blank falls back to the pictures above."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "image_metafield",
      "label": "Banner metafield",
      "info": "The key under the custom namespace. Empty switches the metafield off.",
      "default": "hero_image"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "image_mobile_metafield",
      "label": "Mobile banner metafield",
      "default": "hero_image_mobile"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_scrim",
      "label": "Lighten the photograph behind the words",
      "info": "Off is what the file draws. Turn it on where the collection's own picture is busy or dark under the heading.",
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "scrim_opacity",
      "label": "How much",
      "min": 10,
      "max": 90,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 60,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.show_scrim }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_star",
      "label": "Show the star",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Breadcrumb"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_breadcrumb",
      "label": "Show the breadcrumb",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "parent_title",
      "label": "Step between home and this page",
      "info": "Left empty, the trail runs straight from Home to the collection.",
      "default": "Shop Treats",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.show_breadcrumb }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "parent_link",
      "label": "Where that step goes",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.show_breadcrumb }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:content.layout"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "height",
      "label": "Banner height",
      "info": "A floor. A longer sentence grows the banner rather than spilling out of it.",
      "min": 240,
      "max": 640,
      "step": 10,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 380
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "height_mobile",
      "label": "Banner height on mobile",
      "min": 180,
      "max": 480,
      "step": 10,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 260
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "section_width",
      "label": "t:settings.width",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "page-width",
          "label": "t:options.page"
        },
        {
          "value": "full-width",
          "label": "t:options.full"
        }
      ],
      "default": "page-width"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:content.colors"
    },
    {
      "type": "color_scheme",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "label": "t:settings.color_scheme",
      "default": "scheme-1"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:content.padding"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-start",
      "label": "t:settings.top",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 24
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-end",
      "label": "t:settings.bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Collection hero",
      "category": "t:categories.banners",
      "blocks": {
        "heading": {
          "type": "_ui-heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "<h1><em>Birthday</em> Treats</h1>",
            "heading_size": 48,
            "heading_size_mobile": 32
          }
        },
        "body": {
          "type": "_ui-text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Shop birthday-ready packs, custom image treats, gift boxes, and choose-your-own options.</p>",
            "text_size": 16,
            "text_size_mobile": 14
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading",
        "body"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
